    "id": "polymarket_event_235023",
    "title": "Club Atlético de Madrid vs. Tottenham Hotspur FC",
    "background": "No background available.",
    "resolution_criteria": "In the upcoming game, scheduled for March 10, 2026\nIf Club Atlético de Madrid wins, this market will resolve to \"Yes\".\nOtherwise, this market will resolve to \"No\".\nIf the game is postponed, this market will remain open until the game has been completed.\nIf the game is canceled entirely, with no make-up game, this market will resolve \"No\".\nThis market refers only to the outcome within the first 90 minutes of regular play plus stoppage time.\n\nThe primary resolution source for this market is the official statistics of the event as recognized by the governing body or event organizers. However, if the governing body or event organizers have not published final match statistics within 2 hours after the event's conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead.",
    "outcome": "Club Atlético de Madrid",
    "explanation": "\n# Executive Summary\nClub Atlético de Madrid secured a dominant 5-2 victory over Tottenham Hotspur FC in the first leg of their UEFA Champions League Round of 16 tie on March 10, 2026. The primary causal factor was a disastrous tactical gamble by Tottenham manager Igor Tudor, who unexpectedly started inexperienced backup goalkeeper Antonin Kinsky over regular starter Guglielmo Vicario. Kinsky's high-profile errors in the opening stages led to Tottenham conceding three goals within the first 15 minutes, allowing Atlético to establish an unassailable lead early on and control the remainder of the match.\n\n# Timeline Of Key Events\n- 2026-03-10 (Pre-match): Tottenham manager Igor Tudor makes the controversial decision to drop Guglielmo Vicario and start Antonin Kinsky in goal for the crucial Champions League fixture. [art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43]\n- 2026-03-10 20:00: Match kicks off at the Wanda Metropolitano. [art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43]\n- 2026-03-10 20:06 (6'): Marcos Llorente opens the scoring for Atlético Madrid. [art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43]\n- 2026-03-10 20:14 (14'): Antoine Griezmann doubles the lead following another Kinsky error. [art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43]\n- 2026-03-10 20:15 (15'): Julián Álvarez scores to make it 3-0, compounding Spurs' misery. [art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43]\n- 2026-03-10 20:17 (17'): Antonin Kinsky is substituted off due to his poor performance. [art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43]\n- 2026-03-10 20:22 (22'): Robin Le Normand makes it 4-0 for Atlético. [art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43]\n- 2026-03-10 20:26 (26'): Pedro Porro pulls one back for Tottenham (4-1). [art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43]\n- 2026-03-10 20:55 (55'): Julián Álvarez scores his second goal of the match, restoring a four-goal advantage for Atlético. [art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43]\n- 2026-03-10 21:16 (76'): Dominic Solanke scores for Spurs, resulting in a final score of 5-2. [art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43]\n\n# Causal Chain Analysis\nThe outcome of the match was largely determined by a cascading series of events triggered by a singular managerial decision. \n1. The root cause was Igor Tudor's decision to start backup goalkeeper Antonin Kinsky instead of the more experienced Guglielmo Vicario. [art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43]\n2. This led directly to severe defensive instability for Tottenham, as Kinsky made two critical errors within the first 17 minutes. [art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43]\n3. These errors were ruthlessly punished by Atlético Madrid's attack, resulting in goals from Llorente, Griezmann, and Álvarez, putting Atlético 3-0 up by the 15th minute. [art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43]\n4. The immense early deficit completely disrupted Tottenham's game plan and morale, allowing Atlético to dictate the pace and ultimately secure a comfortable 5-2 victory. [art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43]\n\n# Countervailing Factors\nTottenham showed some resilience despite the catastrophic start. The return of key defenders Micky van de Ven and Cristian Romero [art_general_20260310_007_cc7a7550] provided some stability later in the match. Furthermore, goals from Pedro Porro and Dominic Solanke demonstrated Tottenham's attacking capability. However, these efforts were insufficient to overcome the massive 4-0 deficit conceded in the opening 22 minutes.\n\n# Event Candidate Inventory\n- E1: Igor Tudor starts Antonin Kinsky over Guglielmo Vicario.\n  - date: 2026-03-10\n  - why it matters causally: The foundational tactical error that destabilized Tottenham's defense.\n  - source article IDs: art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43\n\n- E2: Antonin Kinsky commits two major errors leading to goals.\n  - date: 2026-03-10\n  - why it matters causally: Directly resulted in Atlético taking a rapid and insurmountable lead.\n  - source article IDs: art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43\n\n- E3: Atlético Madrid scores three goals in the first 15 minutes.\n  - date: 2026-03-10\n  - why it matters causally: Established the massive advantage that secured the victory.\n  - source article IDs: art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43\n\n# Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Tudor starts Kinsky | art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43 | 2026-03-10 | 1.0 | A highly unusual and impactful managerial decision. |\n| Kinsky makes errors | art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43 | 2026-03-10 | 1.0 | Directly caused the early goals. |\n| Atlético scores 3 early goals | art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43 | 2026-03-10 | 1.0 | The primary mechanism of victory. |\n| Final score 5-2 | art_sports_20260310_005_93686f43 | 2026-03-10 | 1.0 | Ground truth outcome. |\n\n# Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\nThe primary uncertainty is whether Tottenham would have still lost if Guglielmo Vicario had started. Given the quality of Atlético Madrid and their home advantage at the Metropolitano, an Atlético victory was plausible regardless. However, the sheer margin of the early collapse (conceding three goals in 15 minutes) is heavily attributed to Kinsky's inclusion. An alternative path where Vicario started likely would have resulted in a much tighter, lower-scoring contest, potentially altering the match's entire trajectory.\n",
