    "explanation": "\n## Executive Summary\nThe Houthis launched a military action against Israel on March 28, 2026, marking their entry into the broader conflict with Iran. This attack directly led to the market resolving the question to the ground truth outcome. The attack was driven by escalating regional tensions and the Houthis' alignment with Iran, fulfilling their earlier threats.\n\n## Timeline Of Key Events\n- March 10, 2026: Houthis temporarily backtracked on strike threats following US pressure, causing the market to lean \"No\" [art_politics_20260310_004_03766691].\n- March 22, 2026: Escalating conflict between Iran and Israel increased regional instability [art_general_20260322_022_65e7e45a].\n- March 28, 2026: Iranian-backed Houthi rebels claimed responsibility for a direct missile attack on Israel, entering the Iran war [art_general_20260328_019_5b3a6495] [art_politics_20260328_003_650c8c23].\n- March 29-30, 2026: The attack stokes fears of renewed Red Sea shipping strikes and causes Brent crude to surge [art_general_20260329_009_75503599] [art_general_20260330_017_77806722].\n- April 4, 2026: Market resolves based on the late March Houthi attack.\n\n## Causal Chain Analysis\nThe root cause was the broader conflict between Iran and Israel, which escalated in early March. The intermediate mechanism was Iran's activation of its proxy network, leading the Houthis to prepare for action. Despite temporary de-escalation on March 10, the proximate trigger was the intensification of strikes between Iran and Israel around March 22. This resulted in the final outcome on March 28, when the Houthis launched missiles at Israel, fulfilling their strategic commitment to the Axis of Resistance.\n\n## Countervailing Factors\nUS diplomatic and military pressure caused a temporary backtracking by the Houthis on March 10 [art_politics_20260310_004_03766691]. However, this pressure was overwhelmed by the rapid escalation of the core Iran-Israel conflict later in the month.\n\n## Event Candidate Inventory\n- E1\n    - Title: Houthis backtrack on strike threats\n    - Date: 2026-03-10\n    - Why it matters causally: Caused a temporary drop in market expectations for a strike.\n    - Source article IDs: art_politics_20260310_004_03766691\n- E2\n    - Title: Iran strikes near Israel nuclear center\n    - Date: 2026-03-22\n    - Why it matters causally: Escalated the broader conflict, pushing proxies closer to action.\n    - Source article IDs: art_general_20260322_022_65e7e45a\n- E3\n    - Title: Houthi missile attack on Israel\n    - Date: 2026-03-28\n    - Why it matters causally: The direct military action that resolved the market question.\n    - Source article IDs: art_general_20260328_019_5b3a6495, art_politics_20260328_003_650c8c23\n\n## Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Houthis backtrack | art_politics_20260310_004_03766691 | 2026-03-10 | 0.9 | Explains the March 10 dip |\n| Escalation by Iran | art_general_20260322_022_65e7e45a | 2026-03-22 | 0.9 | Explains the March 22 volatility |\n| Houthi strike on Israel | art_general_20260328_019_5b3a6495, art_politics_20260328_003_650c8c23 | 2026-03-28 | 1.0 | The conclusive event |\n\n## Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\nIt remains slightly unclear why the market resolved to \"April 15\" as the ground truth if the attack was clearly on March 28, but the April 15 option might have been a time-bucket or subsequent deadline option in the market that encompassed the March 28 event.\n",
