    "resolution_criteria": "This market will resolve to \"Yes\" if the Russian Armed Forces initiate a drone, missile, or air strike on Kyiv municipality on the listed date Eastern European Time (EET). Otherwise, this market will resolve to \"No\".\n\nFor the purposes of this market, a qualifying \"strike\" is defined as the use of aerial bombs, drones, or missiles (including cruise or ballistic missiles) launched by Russian Armed Forces that impact Kyiv municipality's ground territory.\n\nA strike on any area within the terrestrial territory of the Kyiv municipality counts.\n\nMissiles or drones that are intercepted and surface-to-air missile strikes will not be sufficient for a \"Yes\" resolution, regardless of whether they land on the Kyiv municipality's territory or cause damage.\n\nActions such as artillery fire, small arms fire, FPV or ATGM strikes, ground incursions, naval shelling, cyberattacks, or other operations conducted by the Russian armed forces will not qualify.\n\nThe primary resolution source will be official government/military statements (Ukrainian or Russian), multilateral bodies (UN, etc.), or a consensus of credible reporting from major international media and national broadcasters/newspapers.\n\nIf the date/time of a strike cannot be confirmed by a consensus of credible reporting within 48 hours of this market's end date, it will resolve to \"No\" regardless of whether a strike was later confirmed to have taken place.",
    "outcome": "February 3",
    "explanation": "\n## Executive Summary\nOn the night of February 2-3, 2026, Russia launched a massive combined missile and drone attack on Ukrainian energy infrastructure and residential areas, including significant strikes on the Kyiv municipality. This assault, involving over 450 drones and 70 missiles, was the largest attack of the winter and caused severe damage, widespread blackouts, and disrupted heating for thousands of residents during a severe cold snap. The strikes occurred strategically just prior to scheduled US-brokered peace talks, ending a brief moratorium on targeting energy grids.\n\n## Timeline Of Key Events\n- **February 2, 2026:** Reports surface that Kyiv and other major cities are bracing for renewed strikes, with an air-raid warning issued overnight due to ballistic threats [art_politics_20260202_002_db3fcb96].\n- **February 3, 2026 (01:09):** Ballistic missile threats and drone attacks are confirmed over Kyiv, leading to explosions in the city [art_politics_20260203_005_525eec43].\n- **February 3, 2026:** Significant damage is reported in Kyiv's Dniprovskyi district, including residential high-rises and a kindergarten catching fire, resulting in at least five injuries [art_politics_20260203_005_525eec43].\n- **February 3, 2026:** The attack is characterized as the largest of the winter, cutting heating to over 1,000 apartment blocks in Kyiv during sub-zero temperatures [art_general_20260203_003_f35a8aef].\n- **February 3, 2026:** Analysts note the strikes were a deliberate pressure tactic ahead of upcoming US-brokered peace talks [art_politics_20260202_004_2103043f].\n\n## Causal Chain Analysis\nThe root cause of this specific event was Russia's strategic decision to intensify pressure on Ukraine ahead of impending US-brokered peace negotiations [art_politics_20260202_004_2103043f]. This led to a large-scale mobilization of aerial assets, deploying over 450 drones and 70 missiles aimed primarily at critical energy infrastructure [art_general_20260203_003_f35a8aef]. The proximate trigger for the impact on Kyiv was the successful penetration of Ukraine's air defenses by some of these munitions early on February 3 [art_politics_20260203_005_525eec43]. This directly resulted in the destruction of property, fires, civilian injuries, and significant loss of power and heating for residents in the capital [art_general_20260203_003_f35a8aef].\n\n## Countervailing Factors\nUkraine's air defense systems actively attempted to intercept the incoming drones and missiles. However, the sheer volume of the assault—using swarms of drones combined with ballistic missiles—overwhelmed defensive capabilities in certain areas, allowing several projectiles to impact their targets in Kyiv [art_politics_20260203_005_525eec43].\n\n## Event Candidate Inventory\n- **E1: Russian Strategic Escalation Ahead of Talks**\n  - Date: Early February 2026\n  - Why it matters causally: Provided the motivation and timing for the massive assault.\n  - Source article IDs: art_politics_20260202_004_2103043f\n- **E2: Massive Aerial Bombardment Launch**\n  - Date: February 2-3, 2026\n  - Why it matters causally: The physical action that deployed the weapons towards Kyiv.\n  - Source article IDs: art_general_20260203_003_f35a8aef\n- **E3: Munitions Impacting Kyiv**\n  - Date: February 3, 2026\n  - Why it matters causally: The direct event that fulfilled the criteria of the prediction market question.\n  - Source article IDs: art_politics_20260203_005_525eec43\n\n## Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Largest winter attack with drones/missiles | art_general_20260203_003_f35a8aef | Feb 3, 2026 | 1.0 | Confirms scale of the assault. |\n| Strikes hit residential areas in Kyiv causing injuries | art_politics_20260203_005_525eec43 | Feb 3, 2026 | 1.0 | Direct evidence of the impact. |\n| Strategic timing ahead of peace talks | art_politics_20260202_004_2103043f | Feb 2-3, 2026 | 0.9 | Explains the underlying motivation. |\n\n## Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\nThere was little uncertainty that the strike occurred on February 3 once the events unfolded. The main alternative path earlier on might have been the continuation of the brief moratorium on energy strikes, but Russia's geopolitical calculations to apply maximum leverage before negotiations overrode that possibility.\n",
