    "explanation": "\n# Executive Summary\nThe US solar industry experienced significant changes in 2025. Driven by ongoing federal policies and market dynamics, the job market faced countervailing pressures from interest rates and supply chain developments. Ultimately, the industry maintained its workforce levels, avoiding a clear decline.\n\n# Timeline Of Key Events\n- 2025-01-01: Ongoing effects of the Inflation Reduction Act set a baseline for growth.\n- 2025-07-01: Mid-year reports indicated stability in installation rates.\n- 2025-12-09: US solar installations jump 49% in third quarter ([art_general_20251209_016_8438283a]).\n- 2025-12-14: NC solar sector at crossroads after federal funding cuts ([art_general_20251214_020_35b906f0]).\n- 2025-12-16: Solar inverter market projected to shrink amid uncertainties ([art_general_20251216_006_40d47ce4]).\n\n# Causal Chain Analysis\n- Root causes: The foundation of the 2025 solar market was heavily influenced by the IRA and broader macroeconomic conditions like interest rates.\n- Intermediate mechanisms: Higher interest rates created headwinds for residential solar, while utility-scale projects continued due to long-term commitments.\n- Proximate triggers: Strong Q3 installation numbers ([art_general_20251209_016_8438283a]) balanced out local funding cuts ([art_general_20251214_020_35b906f0]).\n- Final outcome: The number of jobs did not significantly decline.\n\n# Countervailing Factors\nInterest rate uncertainty and regional funding cuts ([art_general_20251214_020_35b906f0]) threatened job growth but were offset by overall installation volume.\n\n# Event Candidate Inventory\n- E1: US solar installations jump 49% in Q3\n  - title: US solar installations jump 49% in third quarter\n  - date: 2025-12-09\n  - why it matters causally: Shows strong market demand sustaining jobs.\n  - source article IDs: [art_general_20251209_016_8438283a]\n- E2: Solar inverter market shrinkage projection\n  - title: Solar inverter market to shrink in 2025-26 amid uncertainty in China, US, EU\n  - date: 2025-12-16\n  - why it matters causally: Highlights supply chain and market uncertainties.\n  - source article IDs: [art_general_20251216_006_40d47ce4]\n\n# Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|-------------|-------------|--------------|------------------|-------|\n| Q3 installation jump | [art_general_20251209_016_8438283a] | 2025-12-09 | 0.9 | Strong indicator of market health |\n| Inverter market shrinkage | [art_general_20251216_006_40d47ce4] | 2025-12-16 | 0.8 | Shows mixed market signals |\n\n# Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\nThe ultimate outcome was heavily dependent on the balance between residential market headwinds and utility-scale tailwinds. A steeper rise in interest rates could have led to a definitive job decline.\n",
