    "id": "polymarket_event_107358",
    "title": "Which companies added to S&P 500 in Q1 2026?",
    "background": "No background available.",
    "resolution_criteria": "The S&P 500 undergoes quarterly reconstitution on the third Friday of March, June, September, and December. The next rebalance is currently scheduled for March 20, 2026.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Yes\" if S&P Global Inc. announces that the listed company will be added to the S&P 500 index by March 31, 2026, 11:59 PM ET. Otherwise, this market will resolve to \"No.\"\n\nTo qualify, the listed ticker must match the announced ticker added to the index.\n\nAn announcement from S&P will qualify for a \"Yes\" resolution, regardless of whether the listed company has actually been added to the S&P 500 index by the resolution date. \n\nThe primary resolution source will be official announcements from S&P Global Inc. (https://www.spglobal.com/en/press/press-release).",
    "outcome": "Ciena (CIEN)",
    "explanation": "\n## Executive Summary\nThe market's prediction for Q1 2026 S&P 500 inclusion centered around Ciena (CIEN), Pure Storage (PSTG), SoFi Technologies (SOFI), and other candidates. In late December 2025, market predictions fluctuated significantly, as investors debated between companies. Ultimately, on February 4, 2026, S&P Dow Jones Indices announced that Ciena Corporation (CIEN) would replace Dayforce in the S&P 500 index. This resulted in the final outcome, driven by Ciena's strong revenue growth fueled by high demand for data center infrastructure and optical networking equipment for generative AI workloads. \n\n## Timeline Of Key Events\n- Late 2025/Early 2026: Various companies, including Pure Storage (PSTG), SoFi Technologies (SOFI), MicroStrategy (MSTR), and Alnylam Pharmaceuticals (ALNY), were considered strong candidates for S&P 500 inclusion, which caused market volatility and lead changes in predictions ([art_finance_20251223_006_20910f7c], [art_finance_20251225_007_f6155bf8], [art_finance_20260108_008_5ab21dd0], [art_finance_20260112_009_34b64b79]).\n- December 2025: Ciena's CEO highlighted that generative AI infrastructure demand would be a major contributor to their 2026 growth, which led to boosted investor sentiment ([art_finance_20260204_003_867edfe7]).\n- February 4, 2026: S&P Dow Jones Indices officially announced that Ciena would replace Dayforce in the S&P 500 index, effective before the open of trading on February 9, 2026 ([art_business_20260204_002_6f1422d4], [art_finance_20260204_003_867edfe7]). Thoma Bravo had recently acquired Dayforce, creating the opening.\n\n## Causal Chain Analysis\nThe root cause of Ciena's inclusion was the booming demand for data center infrastructure to support generative artificial intelligence workloads. This demand caused Ciena's revenue growth to soar, resulting in their market capitalization nearly tripling over the past year ([art_finance_20260204_003_867edfe7]). This strong financial performance positioned Ciena as a prime candidate for S&P 500 inclusion. The proximate trigger for the actual index change was the acquisition of Dayforce by Thoma Bravo, which created a vacancy in the S&P 500. S&P Dow Jones Indices subsequently selected Ciena to fill this vacancy, leading to the final outcome of Ciena joining the index ([art_finance_20260204_003_867edfe7]).\n\n## Countervailing Factors\nOther companies like Pure Storage, SoFi, MicroStrategy, and Alnylam were also strong contenders and saw market support based on their own earnings and strategic positioning. For instance, Alnylam was seen as \"on track\" following positive earnings ([art_finance_20260112_009_34b64b79]). However, Ciena's direct tie to the massive structural tailwind of generative AI infrastructure buildouts overwhelmed these factors, as it made Ciena a more compelling choice for the index committee at that specific time.\n\n## Event Candidate Inventory\n- E1: S&P Dow Jones Indices announces Ciena replacing Dayforce in S&P 500\n  - date: 2026-02-04\n  - why it matters causally: This triggered the official resolution event that confirms the ground truth.\n  - source article IDs: [art_business_20260204_002_6f1422d4], [art_finance_20260204_003_867edfe7]\n- E2: Thoma Bravo acquires Dayforce\n  - date: late 2025 / early 2026\n  - why it matters causally: Created the vacancy in the S&P 500 that Ciena filled, resulting in the inclusion slot.\n  - source article IDs: [art_finance_20260204_003_867edfe7]\n\n## Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Ciena added to S&P 500 replacing Dayforce | [art_business_20260204_002_6f1422d4], [art_finance_20260204_003_867edfe7] | 2026-02-04 | 1.0 | Official S&P announcement |\n| Generative AI demand boosting Ciena's growth | [art_finance_20260204_003_867edfe7] | Dec 2025 / Feb 2026 | 0.9 | CEO statement and financial analysis |\n| Other companies like ALNY were strong candidates | [art_finance_20260112_009_34b64b79] | 2026-01-12 | 0.8 | Market analysis |\n\n## Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\nThe precise timing of inclusion could have varied if Thoma Bravo's acquisition of Dayforce had been delayed or if another S&P 500 component had been removed earlier. Had Ciena's supply chain issues constrained their growth more significantly, another candidate like Pure Storage or SoFi might have been selected instead.\n",
